# Agent Instructions for AI Coding Assistants

## Rule 0: docs/ MUST stay in sync with src/

Editing any `src/*.py` or source file REQUIRES updating its matching `docs/<module>.md` in the same change. The docs are read instead of source to save tokens, so stale docs mislead every future agent. No exceptions; create the doc if missing.

## Rule 1: Targeted tests while patching, fresh suite before commit

After every meaningful change to source or UI, run the smallest relevant check:

```bash
python -m py_compile app.py src/*.py
python tests/test_specific.py
```

For UI changes, also run a Streamlit AppTest:

```bash
python -c 'from streamlit.testing.v1 import AppTest; at = AppTest.from_file("app.py", default_timeout=30); at.run(); assert not at.exception, at.exception'
```

Before every commit touching code, run the full active suite fresh after the last edit:

```bash
make test # or pytest
```

Commit only on 0 failures and record pass counts in `CHANGELOG.md`.

## Universal Engineering Standard

This project adheres to `GOLDEN_STD.md`. If `GOLDEN_STD.md` is missing or outdated, synchronize it from `playloud679/dev_standards`.
